This file documents work/ACTIVE — it is NOT read by any tooling.

work/ACTIVE is a MACHINE-LOCAL, single-line file naming the project THIS Claude
instance is currently working on (e.g. the single line `Viggo-fix`). It is
gitignored on purpose: under the multi-instance operating model each machine runs
its own active project, so a committed pointer would let two instances flip each
other's active project on every push/pull.

Set it for this machine with:

    /project-switch <project-name>

or, equivalently, write the bare project name into work/ACTIVE:

    printf 'Viggo-fix\n' > work/ACTIVE

If work/ACTIVE is missing, flow commands stop and ask you to /project-switch —
they never fall back to another machine's project.
